Python Zero

Flow: Welcome screen → enter name → main menu loop → lessons 1–7 (each with a quiz) → final quiz (unlocked after all 7) → certificate → exit.

Setup
LESSON_PASS_MARK = 2 (out of 3) and FINAL_PASS_MARK = 7 (out of 10).
os clears the screen, time adds animation delays.
Helper functions
Screen: clear_screen runs cls or clear depending on the OS. pause waits for Enter. show_banner prints a centered title between = lines.
Transitions: transition_in and transition_out animate a line growing or shrinking using end="\r" to overwrite the same line.
Display: show_part prints a lesson screen line by line. show_code prints code, with or without line numbers. show_question prints the question header.
Input checks:
has_letters: name must contain at least one letter.
is_number_answer: tells numeric answers from text answers.
get_letter: loops until the user enters A, B, or C.
get_typed_answer: loops until the answer is non-empty and the right type (number vs. text).
show_result: shows Correct or Not quite, plus the explanation.
Question types

Each returns True or False.

multiple_choice: pick A, B, or C and compare to the answer.
fix_error: type the corrected line. Spaces are ignored and ' equals ".
try_code: run the code yourself and type the output. Spaces, commas, and capitals are ignored.
Lessons

Every lesson follows one pattern:

Transition in
Show the lesson parts
Start the quiz with score = 0
Add 1 for each question that returns True
finish_quiz(score) returns pass or fail (2 or more passes)

The final quiz works the same way with 10 questions, but it returns the raw score and the menu decides pass or fail.

Main program
Memory: completed (passed lesson numbers), final_passed, final_score.
Name entry: loops until the name is not empty and has a letter.
Menu loop (while True):
Show the menu with [X] or [ ] for each lesson, and the final quiz as locked, unlocked, or done.
Read the choice. If it isn’t all digits, show an error and loop back.
Convert to int and branch:
1–7: run the lesson. If passed and not already in completed, add it.
8: only runs if all 7 are completed. A score of 7 or more shows the certificate.
0: break ends the program.
Anything else: invalid choice.
